From 0de2ca0037af65fd9bcd1dabff9e1c3096e29466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:13:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_conv: let a type alias in a function argument's pattern
 leave out its generic arguments

bitstream-io 4.10.0 (mdcat 2.18.0) lib.rs:2923, in both endian impls:

    pub type CheckedUnsigned<const MAX: u32, T> = Checked<BitCount<MAX>, T>;
    fn write_bits_checked<const MAX: u32, W, U>(..,
        CheckedUnsigned { count: BitCount { bits }, value }: CheckedUnsigned<MAX, U>,
    ) -> io::Result<()>

Alias expansion fills omitted alias arguments with inference variables only
inside expressions. Argument patterns are visited with the signature,
outside the body, so the pattern's path got none: "<null> error:0:
Mismatched type-generic count in ::bitstream_io::CheckedUnsigned, expected
1 got 0". A struct's own path in the same position already gets
inference variables (visit_pattern_PathBinding).

Expander::visit_pattern now treats every pattern as an inference context.
Typeck unifies the pattern with the argument's declared type, as for any
other pattern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp b/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
index 6557e933..06ba862c 100644
--- a/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
@@ -390,6 +390,16 @@ public:
     {
         static Span sp;
 
+        // A pattern is checked against an inferred type, so its paths can leave out an alias's generic arguments (as
+        // they can a struct's, see `visit_pattern_PathBinding`), even in a function's argument list.
+        // - bitstream-io 4.10.0: `CheckedUnsigned { count, value }: CheckedUnsigned<MAX, U>` as an argument
+        auto saved_in_expr = m_in_expr;
+        m_in_expr = true;
+        visit_pattern_inner(sp, pat);
+        m_in_expr = saved_in_expr;
+    }
+    void visit_pattern_inner(const Span& sp, ::HIR::Pattern& pat)
+    {
         ::HIR::Visitor::visit_pattern(pat);
 
         TU_MATCH_HDRA( (pat.m_data), {)
